K3 -- make a lattice-polarized K3 surface
*****************************************

  * Usage: 
        K3(g,d,n)
        K3(g,d,n,CoefficientRing=>K)
  * Inputs:
      * g, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * CoefficientRing => ..., default value ZZ/65521
      * Singular => ..., default value null
      * Strategy => ..., default value null
      * Verbose => ..., default value false
  * Outputs:
      * a *note K3 surface: LatticePolarizedK3surface, defined over $K$ with
        rank 2 lattice defined by the intersection matrix $\begin{pmatrix} 2g-2
        & d \\ d & n \end{pmatrix}$

Description
===========

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : K3(6,1,-2)                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = K3 surface with rank                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|     -- (1,0): K3 surface                                                    |
|     -- (2,0): K3 surface                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : Lattice-polarized K3                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|2 lattice defined by the intersection matrix: | 10 1  |                      |
|                                              | 1  -2 |                      |
|of genus 6 and degree 10 containing rational curve of degree 1 (GM fourfold) |
|of genus 21 and degree 40 containing rational curve of degree 2              |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|surface                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

